## Codebase Discoveries
The real cause was Homebrew's bundle-version check for auto_updates casks. In the installed source, /opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cask/cask.rb defines Cask#outdated_version and auto_updates_bundle_outdated?, and gates the check on Homebrew::EnvConfig.upgrade_auto_updates_casks?. /opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/env_config.rb defines HOMEBREW_NO_UPGRADE_AUTO_UPDATES_CASKS and uses it to disable the default upgrade behavior. The opt-out does not override --greedy or --greedy-auto-updates. The full update run refreshed vendored skills without introducing tracked changes before the external rules fetch failed.

